messages.content:
I couldn't find the NaMaster sacc file, so nothing has been computed yet: no TJPCov config, no covariance, no Knox comparison and no chi2.

There are no earlier turns or tool ledger in this conversation that record a NaMaster measurement. I tried the default path, `/Users/nramachandra/hep-genesis-testing/projects/ramp-desc/runs/261021_171201/namaster.sacc`, and got "sacc file not found". I'm not going to guess other filenames or make up results.

Two ways forward:

1. **You give me the path** to the NaMaster sacc. Ideally also the `<name>_fields.json` and the mask, so I can read the effective f_sky, n_gal and bias directly. I would then:
   - check the mask's effective f_sky;
   - inspect the sacc;
   - drop the B-modes and rename tracers to the firecrown convention;
   - write and run the TJPCov FourierGaussianFsky config;
   - attach a plain Knox covariance on the same file;
   - compare the two covariances;
   - build the firecrown likelihood and report chi2 at the input cosmology, plus whether the covariance is positive definite.

2. **I regenerate the test bed from scratch** (simulated masked maps, then the NaMaster bandpowers) and run the same chain. The run is local and takes minutes at nside 128. Unless you specify otherwise, I'd use:
   - one shear tracer, src0: z_mean 0.9, n_gal 8 arcmin^-2, sigma_e 0.26;
   - one density tracer, lens0: z_mean 0.5, bias 1.6, n_gal 4 arcmin^-2;
   - f_sky 0.25 and vanilla ΛCDM.

Which do you want? If option 2, tell me any tracer setup or cosmology you'd like changed.
